<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhodope Mountains</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rhodopes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rhodope Mountains are a range in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, mostly in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> with their southern slopes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Wooded and rich in ores, they were home to Thracian peoples such as the Bessi and hold rock sanctuaries such as Perperikon; legend makes them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of Orpheus. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> they were a frontier zone between Bulgaria and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>.</p></div>
